Third-Party Components in Released SD Card Images
===================================================

The `.img` files produced by this builder are combined works. They are NOT
entirely covered by the GPL-2.0-or-later license of this repository's scripts.

Release and CI artifact downloads include LICENSE, this NOTICE,
LICENSE_GPL-2.0-or-later.txt, LICENSE_TFA.txt, SOURCE_INFO_TFA.txt,
SOURCE_OFFER_U_BOOT.txt, and SOURCE_INFO_R2S_KERNEL.txt alongside the image.

Components fetched or built at image-creation time include:

Trusted Firmware-A BL31 (BSD-3-Clause)
--------------------------------------
- Source: https://github.com/ARM-software/arm-trusted-firmware.git
- Tag: v2.15.0 (commit da738d5eae93af342fdc4995dd3c05acb4c9d757)
- Built from source during image creation (PLAT=rk3328)
- License and source information: LICENSE_TFA.txt, SOURCE_INFO_TFA.txt

U-Boot (GPL-2.0-or-later)
-------------------------
- Source: https://source.denx.de/u-boot/u-boot.git
- Tag: v2026.07 (commit ece349ade2973e220f524ce59e59711cc919263f, signed tag)
- Built from source during image creation (nanopi-r2s-rk3328_defconfig)
- Host-tool compatibility patch: vendor/patches/u-boot/pylibfdt-swig-4.5.patch
- Produces the mainline Rockchip `u-boot-rockchip.bin` image used on the SD card
- GPL source information: SOURCE_OFFER_U_BOOT.txt

NanoPi R2S minimal kernel package (GPL-2.0-only)
------------------------------------------------
- Package: linux-nanopi-r2s-minimal
- Source/package repository: https://github.com/therealcoder1337/nanopi-r2s-kernel-arch
- Used only by the `nanopi-r2s-arch-minimal-kernel-*` image variant
- Source archive and merged kernel config are published with the matching
  kernel package release
- Source information: SOURCE_INFO_R2S_KERNEL.txt

Arch Linux ARM root filesystem (mixed licenses)
------------------------------------------------
- Project: https://archlinuxarm.org
- Source tarball: http://os.archlinuxarm.org/os/ArchLinuxARM-aarch64-latest.tar.gz
- Package build/source metadata: https://github.com/archlinuxarm/PKGBUILDs
- Build verifies the tarball with GPG key 68B3537F39A313B3E574D06777193F152BDBE6A6
  (see vendor/alarmsigning.gpg in the source repository)
- The image contains many packages (kernel, userspace) under GPL, LGPL, and
  other open-source licenses; per-package license texts are on the device under
  /usr/share/licenses

